{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "map.schema.json",
  "title": "Carte / grille de lieux",
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "name": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "grid_size": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "rows": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1 },
        "cols": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1 }
      },
      "required": ["rows", "cols"]
    },
    "movement": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "default": "orthogonal",
      "$comment": "Une seule valeur apparaît dans ton template sans liste d'alternatives en commentaire, donc pas d'enum forcé ici (je ne veux pas inventer 'diagonal'/'libre' à ta place). Confirme si tu veux verrouiller les valeurs possibles."
    },
    "map": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 1,
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "place": { "$ref": "common.schema.json#/$defs/slug" },
          "col": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 },
          "row": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 }
        },
        "required": ["place", "col", "row"]
      }
    },
    "lieu_infranchissable": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "Optionnel : liste des cases infranchissables sans lieu.",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "row": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 },
          "col": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 },
          "reason": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 }
        },
        "required": ["row", "col", "reason"]
      }
    }
  },
  "required": ["name", "grid_size", "movement", "map", "lieu_infranchissable"],
  "$comment": "Non vérifié par ce schema : que row/col de 'map' et 'lieu_infranchissable' restent dans les bornes de grid_size, et qu'il n'y a pas de collision entre une case de 'map' et une case de 'lieu_infranchissable'. À valider côté application."
}